<section class="section">
  <div class="container faq-stage">
    <div class="faq-header">
      <h2 class="section-title section-title-glow">Executive coaching — common questions</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-grid">
      <details class="faq-card" open>
        <summary>What is executive career coaching?</summary>
        <p>Executive career coaching is strategic career support for Directors, VPs, SVPs, C-suite, and board-level professionals targeting senior leadership roles. It goes beyond resume help — covering executive positioning, leadership narrative, board-level communication, executive search strategy, and offer negotiation for roles paying $150K–$350K+. Unlike general career coaching, executive coaching works on how your scope, decisions, and leadership impact read at the organizational level, not just the functional level.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-card">
        <summary>When do executives need a career coach?</summary>
        <p>Four situations: (1) You are moving from IC or functional leader to executive for the first time. (2) You are stuck below VP or C-suite despite the scope you are operating at. (3) You have been in the same company for 5+ years and your market signal has atrophied. (4) You have a live executive search and need to sharpen your story, interview performance, or offer negotiation. The common thread is a gap between the role you are capable of and what the market currently understands about you.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-card">
        <summary>How is executive career coaching different from regular career coaching?</summary>
        <p>Three key differences: (1) The positioning work focuses on organizational impact, P&L ownership, and leadership at scale — not individual contributions. (2) The interview work covers executive presentations, board-level communication, stakeholder alignment stories, and multi-round executive interview loops. (3) The offer work involves equity, RSU vesting, relocation, title negotiation, and compensation packages that are often more complex than individual contributor offers.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-card">
        <summary>How long does executive coaching take?</summary>
        <p>For executives with active searches, the most impactful engagement is 4–8 weeks of intensive work: positioning, materials, interview prep, and offer strategy. For longer-range moves — a VP preparing to position for C-suite — engagements typically run 90 days. Most executives who start with a strategy call can scope the right engagement in the first session.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-card">
        <summary>What does executive coaching cost?</summary>
        <p>Executive coaching at Askia is priced based on scope — the level you are targeting, the complexity of the search, and the services needed. Resume-only and LinkedIn-only work is available at lower tiers. Full-scope executive advisory engagements covering materials, interview prep, and offer strategy are priced for the scope and the compensation band being targeted. Current pricing is discussed on the free strategy call.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-card">
        <summary>Do you work with first-time executives?</summary>
        <p>Yes — this is one of the most common engagements. First-time VPs and C-suite leaders face a specific challenge: their materials and interview stories are still written for their previous functional role, not for the organizational scope they are targeting. The coaching rebuilds the story at the right level, which is often the single biggest unlock in a stalled executive search.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

